            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for egotism, then the Gujarati for to get used to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: કાયર",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કાયર — kāyar — \"cowardly\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કાયર માણસ જોખમ જોઈને ભાગી જાય છે. kāyar māṇas jokham joīne bhāgī jāy che. A coward runs away at the sight of danger."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કાયર (kāyar) is inherited from Sanskrit kātara, \"confused, discouraged, cowardly\"; CDIAL lists the Gujarati word, \"timid\" (CDIAL 3027)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
