          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ખમીર (khamīr) is usually traced to Arabic xamīr, \"leaven\", through Persian. Gujarati also uses it for the spirit that makes a person rise to a challenge, probably a picture of dough rising."
            }
          ]
        },
